    {
      "text": "he said to Jeroboam … I will … give ten tribes to thee, 1 Kgs. 11:31. Israel rebelled against the house of David, 1 Kgs. 12:19. none … followed the house of David, but … Judah only, 1 Kgs. 12:20. he shall root up Israel out of this good land, 1 Kgs. 14:15. king of Assyria … carried Israel away into Assyria, 2 Kgs. 17:6. Lord rejected … Israel, 2 Kgs. 17:20 (18:11). shall Ephraim be broken, that it be not a people, Isa. 7:8 (2 Ne. 17:8). spoil of Samaria shall be taken away, Isa. 8:4 (2 Ne. 18:4). Who gave Jacob for a spoil, and Israel to the robbers, Isa. 42:24. I will say to the north, Give up, Isa. 43:6. these shall come from … the north, Isa. 49:12 (1 Ne. 21:12). For a small moment have I forsaken thee, Isa. 54:7. proclaim these words toward the north, Jer. 3:12. come together out of the land of the north, Jer. 3:18. brought up … Israel from the land of the north, Jer. 16:15. which led … Israel out of the north country, Jer. 23:8. I will bring them from the north country, Jer. 31:8. Israel shall surely go into captivity, Amos 7:17. sift the house of Israel among all nations, Amos 9:9. flee from the land of the north, Zech. 2:6. scattered them with a whirlwind among all the nations, Zech. 7:14. I will sow them among the people, Zech. 10:9. I will bring them … out of Assyria, Zech. 10:10.",
